# PinoyBusinessPOS React Button Standard

For PinoyBusinessPOS React button / CTA / icon-control work:

1. Follow `src/Products/PinoyBusinessPOS/Docs/UI/exits-button-standard.md` (authoritative contract).
2. Reuse the shared ExItS `Button` in `ExItS.PinoyBusinessPOS.React/src/components/ui/button.tsx`.
3. Do **not** invent local visual button systems or third-party visual button skins when shared `Button` can express the action.
4. Request buttons with the locked playground command `ext btn` (see `exits-button-standard.md`). Example: `ext btn primary outline`, `ext btn icon ghost`, `ext btn compact star`. Do **not** invent a new shorthand. Map that command onto the shared `Button` (`intent` / `appearance` / `shape`; icon only uses `size="icon"`).
5. The Button playground on `/ui-standards` → Buttons is the locked visual reference. Preserve Preferences theme (light / dark / system). Density words in the command are `tight`, `compact`, `comfort`, and `relaxed`; Standard density follows the current preference height.
6. Icon-only controls (`ext btn icon`) need an accessible name and tooltip. `shape="round"` is for circular icon-only.
7. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (no unnecessary lift / scale / rotate).
8. Cancel → `CircleX`; Cancel & return → `CornerUpLeft`; Close-only → `X`; Back → `ArrowLeft`.
9. Explicit task overrides take precedence over standard defaults. Domain correctness and accessibility remain mandatory.

## Default look (mandatory — agents get this wrong)

When creating a button, **defaults must look finished and readable**, not washed or clipped.

| Rule | Do | Do not |
|------|----|--------|
| Primary CTA | `intent="primary" appearance="solid"` (enabled = filled brand + `primary-foreground`) | Soft/tinted primary fill with white label; custom pastel backgrounds |
| Size | Always pass a **valid** size: `sm` · `default` · `large` · `icon` | Omit sizing or invent sizes the CVA does not define (missing height/padding → cramped/clipped) |
| Disabled | Rely on shared `Button` disabled chrome (muted surface + muted text, full opacity) | Extra `opacity-*` / `className` fades that wash white text on faded primary |
| Gated confirm | Keep primary solid; `disabled` until valid — label stays readable | Leave Confirm looking like a pale unreadable pill as the “default” state |
| Secondary chips | `appearance="outline"` (or ghost Cancel); do not compete with Confirm | Multiple solid primaries in one row |
| Contrast | Enabled primary must meet readable contrast for the active primary palette | White text on light/washed blue (or any low-contrast primary) |

**Anti-pattern (forbidden):** primary solid + blanket opacity fade → white label on faded brand. That is the “Confirm inspection” bad default.

Keep detailed rules in the markdown standard — do not invent conflicting variants, motion APIs, or colors here.
Visual reference: `/ui-standards` → Buttons.
